<h2>Segment 202 &mdash; harsh words and the environment</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s202S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w1">ngag rtsub po</span>&#x27;i ni, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w2">sa phyogs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w3">sdong dum</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w4">tsher ma</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w5">rdo</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w6">gseg ma</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w7">gyo mo</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w8">mang ba</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w9">rtsub pa</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s202w10">mdangs mi snum pa</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w11">&#x27;bab chu</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w12">mtsho</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w13">lteng ka</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w14">med pa</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w15">skams</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w16">tshva</span> rgo dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w17">dgon dung</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w18">tha chad</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w19">sdig pa can</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w20">sa gzhi</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s202w21">&#x27;jigs pa&#x27;i rgyu</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w22">mang po</span> dang ldan pa dang</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s202S">Because you have spoken <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w1">harsh words</span>, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w2">ground</span> where you live is covered with obstacles like the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w3">trunks of fallen trees</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w4">thorns</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w5">stones</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w6">clods of dirt</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w8">lots</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w7">sharp broken pieces of glass</span>; it&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w9">rough</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s202w10">dreary</span>; <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w14">no</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w11">streams</span>, or <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w12">lakes</span>, or <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w13">springs of water</span>; the whole <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w20">earth</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w15">parched</span>, poisoned with <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w16">salt</span> and borax, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w17">burning hot</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w18">useless</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w19">threatening</span>; a place where there are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s202w22">many</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s202w21">things to fear</span>.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Provisional machine alignment by Codex (Tibetan-first independent proposal). Original GMR English and ACIP-derived Wylie preserved. mdangs mi snum pa is retained as the complete privative phrase rendered dreary; 'jigs pa'i rgyu as the fear-causes recast things to fear. No members are inferred from these phrases. The HGM glossary supports gyo mo, lteng ka, and dgon dung with this row's expanded renderings. rgo is omitted: the glossary's poisoned does not settle the distributed poisoned with salt and borax. tshva owns only salt. Supplied participants, articles, auxiliaries and whole remain unwrapped; conjunctions, genitives, ni, and the existential ldan pa frame are omitted. This is a proposal, not human-approved correspondence.</div>
